  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Friday)\nIssued at 212 PM CST SAT NOV 7 2026\n\nMostly clear and calm conditions will allow for prime radiational\ncooling overnight tonight. Lots of forecast lows tonight in the\n30s across central Alabama, including mid 30s in many areas.\nDecided to pull the trigger on a Frost Advisory overnight across\nthe whole area, as there are bound to be microclimates that will\nsee near ground air temperatures near freezing. We'll probably see\na repeat of these conditions tomorrow night as well.\n\nWe will remain dry through the start of the upcoming work week,\nwith surface high pressure in control. An upper level shortwave\ntrough is forecast to scoot across the southern tier of the nation\non Wednesday, which could help squeeze out a few showers Wednesday\ninto early Thursday. This is quickly followed by another larger \nupper shortwave that digs into the southeast states and helps \ndrive a cold front through our area late Thursday. More cold \ntemperatures filter in behind this front, perhaps even colder than\nthe present system by a few degrees. \n\n/61/",
